From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:53:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: dualsense mode, the controller as the DualSense a PC
 finds

With [input] mode = dualsense the game finds the title's controller as
the USB DualSense (054c:0ce6) Windows finds, through SetupAPI and HID,
DirectInput or raw input, with its touchpad, motion sensors, rumble,
light bar and adaptive triggers.

- wine/ps5/input/pw_dualsense.h: the DualSense's USB reports (input 1,
  output 2, the feature reports SDL and games ask for), its report
  descriptor, and its trigger effects in libScePad's terms.
- The sink keeps the whole controller (pw_wine_set_dualsense,
  pw_wine_dualsense) and the game's output reports
  (pw_wine_dualsense_report, pw_wine_dualsense_output); ntdll.prx
  exports them.
- Patch 0475: xinput1_3 makes the device in the game's process (a
  device manager, the device's HID interface and instance in volatile
  registry keys, a thread answering its I/O as hidclass.sys does);
  0476: ntdll loads xinput1_3 at the start in this mode; 0474:
  wow64win converts the INPUT of a hardware message, without which a
  32-bit game's raw input arrived as message 0. Both Wine builds stage
  pw_dualsense.h beside xinput's Unix library; wow64win joins the
  patched PE modules.
- The title sets PW_DUALSENSE=1, turns the motion sensors on, publishes
  the pad with its touchpad, motion and time (pw_wine_dualsense_state)
  and applies what the game sends: the motors, and with PC5 the light
  bar and the triggers' effects.

Tested on the PC's Wine with the title's side stood in for: SetupAPI,
cfgmgr32, HID attributes, strings, preparsed data and caps, feature
and input reports, queued, waiting and cancelled reads, writes and
output reports, raw input devices and 250 reports a second, DirectInput
enumeration, in 64- and 32-bit processes, and nothing without the mode.
