+## DualSense
+
+A profile's `[input] mode = dualsense` makes the controller the DualSense a
+PC finds plugged in by USB (`054c:0ce6`). The title sets `PW_DUALSENSE=1`,
+publishes the whole controller to its sink (`pw_wine_set_dualsense`: buttons,
+sticks, triggers, the touchpad's fingers, motion, the sample's time) and
+applies what comes back (`pw_wine_dualsense_output`: motors, light bar, the
+triggers' effects, which libScePad's `scePadSetTriggerEffect` takes).
+
+A Windows driver would make the device in `winedevice.exe`, which a title
+cannot start. Patch 0475 makes it in the game's own process instead, in
+xinput1_3 (`dualsense.c`), which ntdll loads at the start in this mode (0476):
+
+- It creates a device manager and a device (`\Device\PwDualSense`) in the
+  server, the symbolic link of its HID interface, and the registry keys plug
+  and play leaves for a HID collection: the instance under
+  `Enum\HID\VID_054C&PID_0CE6&MI_03` and the interface under
+  `DeviceClasses\{4d1e55b2-...}`, enabled. They are volatile and go when the
+  process ends.
+- A thread answers the device's I/O the way ntoskrnl and hidclass.sys do:
+  `get_next_device_request` takes each call, and reads that wait are
+  completed later with `set_irp_result`. Each open file has a queue of input
+  reports (32, resizable), which the thread fills 250 times a second. It
+  answers the HID ioctls hidclass.sys does (attributes, strings, preparsed
+  data, the queue, feature, input and output reports, Wine's raw input
+  handle), and also sends each report on as raw input.
+- The preparsed data is hidparse.sys's own (`dualsense_hid.c` builds its code
+  with the heap in place of the pool).
+- The reports are the Unix library's: `wine/ps5/input/pw_dualsense.h`,
+  staged beside `unixlib.c` by both Wine builds, makes input report 1 from
+  the sink's state (`pw_wine_dualsense`), passes output report 2 to the sink
+  (`pw_wine_dualsense_report`) and answers the feature reports SDL and games
+  ask for (calibration, pairing, firmware). `pw_dualsense_trigger` turns an
+  output report's trigger effects into libScePad's.
+- XInput sees no controller in this mode; without `PW_DUALSENSE=1`, or
+  outside a title, nothing changes.
+
+A 32-bit game's raw input needs patch 0474, so `wow64win` is among the
+patched PE modules (x86_64 only).
+
 To use it on the console:
 - stage `xinput1_3.prx` beside `ntdll.prx`;
 - replace the runtime's xinput DLLs in `lib/wine/i386-windows` and
