diff --git a/wine/patches/0474-wow64win-convert-the-input-of-a-hardware-message.patch b/wine/patches/0474-wow64win-convert-the-input-of-a-hardware-message.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..378c515
--- /dev/null
+++ b/wine/patches/0474-wow64win-convert-the-input-of-a-hardware-message.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
+Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:40:00 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH] wow64win: Convert the input of a hardware message.
+
+NtUserSendHardwareInput passes an INPUT, whose union is 8-byte aligned
+in 64-bit code and 4-byte aligned in 32-bit code, but the thunk handed
+the 32-bit structure on as it was: the message read as 0 and the server
+queued a message the receiving thread could not process ("unknown
+message type 0"). The input is converted as NtUserSendInput's are.
+
+In a PS5 title the DualSense of dualsense mode (patch 0475) runs in the
+game's process, which for a 32-bit game is a WoW64 one; its raw input
+reaches the game only with this.
+---
+ dlls/wow64win/user.c |   28 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
+ 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
+
+diff --git a/dlls/wow64win/user.c b/dlls/wow64win/user.c
+index 92c1877..bb82d52 100644
